OmniSigil::initializeWithMultiplexer
├── given a well-formed config
│   ├── it should emit SigilSet(id, multiplexer, account)
│   └── it should store the config so a later check finds it
├── given an empty expression tree (no nodes)
│   └── it should revert with EmptyExpressionTree
├── given a root node index out of bounds
│   └── it should revert with RootNodeIndexOutOfBounds
├── given more rules than MAX_RULES (128)
│   └── it should revert with TooManyRules
├── given more nodes than MAX_NODES (256)
│   └── it should revert with TooManyNodes
├── given a leaf node referencing a rule index out of bounds
│   └── it should revert with RuleIndexOutOfBounds
└── given an operator node referencing a child index out of bounds
    ├── when a NOT node points past the last node
    │   └── it should revert with NodeChildIndexOutOfBounds
    └── when an AND node points past the last node
        └── it should revert with NodeChildIndexOutOfBounds
